history.idea:
Keep the three stages unchanged for the wiki survivors (call the list W, seeded shuffle). Add a capped warm-up prefix of clean general English prose, used only if W is short of the budget, and build the full T-token list explicitly so the run ends on in-domain text.

1. Count gpt2 tokens of W with tiktoken (or estimate as characters / 4 if that is too slow). Call it nW. If nW >= 0.75*T, return W exactly as now.

2. Otherwise build a prose set P from documents not in W and not rejected by stage 2 as shuffled wiki articles (exclude anything starting with '= ' or with standalone ','/'.' token fraction >= 0.04). A document enters P only if it passes all of these:
- fewer than 2% of lines contain code or spam markers ('{', '};', 'import ', 'http', 'cheap', 'coupon', 'discount', 'best price');
- at least 85% of characters are alphabetic or spaces;
- at least 200 words long;
- not character-scrambled: build the vocabulary of lowercased, punctuation-stripped words from target_sample, and require at least 75% of the document's alphabetic words (first 1,000 words) to be in that vocabulary;
- not a duplicate by the hash of the normalised first 400 characters.

3. Rank P by that in-vocabulary fraction, descending. Take documents from the top until the prefix reaches min(0.25*T, T - nW) tokens.

4. Return prefix (seeded shuffle) + W + W reshuffled with the same rng, repeated until the total is at least T tokens. The trainer then sees the prose first and spends all remaining steps, including the last ones, on wiki text.
